ompetence, positive crew atmosphere, but communication difficulty and egocentric. Candidate B has high reliability, stress handling, but attitude issues and weak memory for numbers (attention). Candidate D strong technical and responsibility but hot temper and know-it-all. Candidate A strong technical and leadership but no crew cooperation evidence, show-off, not open to ideas.\n\nProbably Candidate C still seems strongest overall, but we need to consider communication difficulty. Since we lack evidence of C's communication under stress, we could suggest that as next step. Our vote could be provisional for C, but we can also note uncertainty.\n\nThus: Public message: Summarize that C shows calmness, technical competence, decision quality, positive crew atmosphere, but we lack evidence on communication under stress; propose to probe that. Vote for C.\n\nLet's output."}
